<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Why Mobile Homes Settle in Dunnellon</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>Dunnellon's ground is mostly deep sand over limestone, and the water table runs high near the Rainbow River and the Withlacoochee. Sand doesn't hold a pier the way firmer soil does. When it gets saturated in the summer rainy season and then dries out, it compacts unevenly, and the piers under your home sink at different rates. That's why one corner drops while the rest of the home stays put.</p><p>Age plays a part too. A lot of homes in the Rainbow Springs area and Rainbow Lakes Estates went in during the 1970s and 80s, back when setup standards were looser. Piers were often set on thin pads or right on the sand, and forty-plus years of Florida weather has taken its toll. None of this means your home is in danger. It means it needs a relevel, which is routine work with real fixes.</p><p>The good news is that a proper relevel addresses the cause, not just the symptom. We check pad size and condition at every pier, add or upgrade pads where the sand has swallowed them, and set steel shims that won't crush or rot. Curious what that runs? Our <a href="/mobile-home-leveling-cost/">leveling cost guide</a> breaks down real numbers.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Moisture Under Riverside Homes</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>The number one thing we find under Dunnellon homes isn't a leveling problem at all. It's moisture. Homes near the rivers sit over damp ground most of the year, and once the vapor barrier tears or sags, that humidity goes straight into the insulation and subfloor. Soft spots in the floor, a musty smell, and buckling vinyl are the usual giveaways.</p><p>Moisture and leveling feed each other. A damp underbelly rots shims and softens the ground under piers, which speeds up settling. Then the settling opens gaps in the skirting, which lets in more moisture. Breaking that cycle usually means releveling and sealing up the <a href="/vapor-barrier-ocala/">vapor barrier</a> in the same visit, which saves you a second service call.</p><p>If your floors feel spongy or you can smell dampness inside, don't wait on it. We'll crawl the full underbelly, photograph what we find, and give you a straight answer about what actually needs fixing and what can wait.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Serving Dunnellon and Western Marion County</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>We cover all of Dunnellon and the surrounding area, including Rainbow Springs, Rainbow Lakes Estates, Romeo, and the neighborhoods along US 41 and County Road 484. We also work just across the county line in Citrus Springs. If you're closer to the middle of the county, we have crews in <a href="/mobile-home-leveling-belleview/">Belleview</a> and <a href="/mobile-home-leveling-summerfield/">Summerfield</a> too.</p><p>A lot of our Dunnellon calls come from home sales and insurance renewals. Four-point inspections and wind mitigation reports flag out-of-level frames, loose tie-downs, and damaged vapor barriers, and insurers want them fixed on a deadline. We keep a 24/7 line open for exactly those situations, and every job comes with written documentation your insurer or buyer's inspector will accept.</p><p>Estimates are free and in writing, and we're licensed and insured. Call (352) 247-3105 or email info@ocalalevelpros.com and we'll get eyes under your home, usually within a few days.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:72px 24px;background:#F5F0E4;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3.5vw,36px);margin:0 0 32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DCC8;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16332C;margin:0 0 10px;">How much does mobile home leveling cost in Dunnellon?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Most single-wides in Dunnellon run in the same range as the rest of Marion County, though homes on soft riverside sand sometimes need extra pads or pier work, which adds to the total. We give you a firm written price after we've been under the home, not a guess over the phone. Our <a href="/mobile-home-leveling-cost/">cost guide</a> has real numbers to help you budget.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DCC8;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16332C;margin:0 0 10px;">My home is near the Rainbow River. Does the high water table make leveling harder?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">It changes how we do the job, but it doesn't stop us. On saturated sandy ground we use larger pads to spread the load so piers stop sinking, and we pay extra attention to the vapor barrier since moisture is almost always part of the picture. Homes right by the river often benefit from a moisture inspection at the same time as the relevel.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DCC8;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16332C;margin:0 0 10px;">How often do Dunnellon mobile homes need releveling?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">On the sandy soil out here, every 3 to 5 years is a reasonable check-in, and sooner if you notice sticking doors or sloping floors. Older homes in Rainbow Lakes Estates and Rainbow Springs that have never been releveled are usually overdue. A quick inspection tells you where you stand, and ours are free.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E4DCC8;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16332C;margin:0 0 10px;">Can you fix what my 4-point inspection flagged before my insurance deadline?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Yes, that's one of the most common jobs we do in Dunnellon. Inspectors flag out-of-level frames, corroded tie-downs, and torn vapor barriers, and we can usually handle all three in one visit. We keep a 24/7 line at (352) 247-3105 for pre-closing and insurance deadlines, and you get written documentation for your insurer when the work is done.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
